    "result_text": "All 17 tests pass (across Cp01\u2013Cp09), including the new Cp09 test, and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment rule for owner creation. On `POST /api/owners`, each owner is assigned a code formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where `LAST3` is the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` and `NNNN` is a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current number of owners.\n\nChanges made:\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter, so the value is stored and read back on `GET`.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `assignCustomerCode(owner)` to `addOwner`, computing `LAST3` from `lastName` and `NNNN = findAllOwners().size() + 1`, formatted via `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", ...)`. It runs before the owner is saved, so the count reflects existing owners only.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field (MapStruct maps it by name from the entity) and it appears in the JSON.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table. This is required because the test profile (`hsqldb`) runs with `ddl-auto=none` and loads schema from SQL; the others were updated for consistency.\n\nThe Cp09 test verifies both the format (`SMI-`, `JON-` prefixes) and that the global sequence increments by exactly one between consecutive creates \u2014 both hold.",
